WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.757 --> 00:00:04.958
Hi there!

2
00:00:11.163 --> 00:00:13.965
there! Who are you?

3
00:00:13.985 --> 00:00:17.348
I'm a moose.

4
00:00:19.129 --> 00:00:21.491
Moose are the biggest kind of deer.

5
00:00:24.514 --> 00:00:25.575
Where do you live?

6
00:00:26.956 --> 00:00:29.538
Moose live in cold parts of the world.

7
00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:31.880
We like forests.

8
00:00:33.804 --> 00:00:37.266
We stay near lakes, ponds, or streams.

9
00:00:39.308 --> 00:00:40.369
Can you swim?

10
00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:44.051
Yes, we're great swimmers.

11
00:00:45.672 --> 00:00:47.634
We can also run fast.

12
00:00:50.536 --> 00:00:51.897
It's cold here!

13
00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:55.019
Moose love the cold.

14
00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.681
Our fur keeps us warm.

15
00:01:00.382 --> 00:01:02.504
Our hooves help us walk in snow.

16
00:01:05.672 --> 00:01:06.852
What do you eat?

17
00:01:08.733 --> 00:01:09.993
Moose don't eat meat.

18
00:01:11.514 --> 00:01:15.515
We eat twigs, bark, leaves, and pinecones.

19
00:01:17.296 --> 00:01:19.636
We also eat plants that grow in water.

20
00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:23.998
You have big antlers!

21
00:01:25.638 --> 00:01:27.719
My antlers fall off each year.

22
00:01:29.239 --> 00:01:31.680
Then they grow back—even bigger.

23
00:01:33.248 --> 00:01:35.930
We use antlers to find mates and fight.

24
00:01:38.312 --> 00:01:39.513
Who do you fight?

25
00:01:40.854 --> 00:01:42.435
Male moose fight each other.

26
00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:45.537
We also fight enemies.

27
00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:50.981
Bears, wolves, and cougars hunt us.

28
00:01:55.524 --> 00:01:57.045
I'm going for a swim now.

29
00:01:58.486 --> 00:01:59.547
I'll see you later.

30
00:02:02.062 --> 00:02:03.254
Good-bye, Moose!
